<mxfile host="datalab" type="device" pages="5">
  <diagram id="xf-p1" name="1 - Context">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1700" pageHeight="870" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="c1" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FF3621;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="40" width="54" height="5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c2" value="&lt;b&gt;datalab · Config-Driven Medallion Framework · ONE YAML artifact per table → Lakeflow SDP&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=24;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="54" width="1620" height="38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c3" value="A medallion (bronze → silver → gold) lakehouse framework where the target table IS the unit of work. Author its YAML artifact; the framework generates the pyspark.pipelines datasets, the dqx quality gates, and the AUTO CDC flows. Ships as a Declarative Automation Bundle deployed by GitHub OIDC CI/CD." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13.5;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="98" width="1620" height="48" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c4" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:14px;&#x27;&gt;WHAT EXISTS TODAY&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Framework: the external &lt;tt&gt;datalab&lt;/tt&gt; dependency (the datalab-framework repo): reusable, zero domain code&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Two reference domains: &lt;tt&gt;projects/customer_sales/&lt;/tt&gt; (bronze → silver (AUTO CDC SCD1) → gold, dqx valid/quarantine, edge jobs + notebook) and &lt;tt&gt;projects/sales/&lt;/tt&gt; (pipeline-only feature showcase)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Three authoring lanes: SDP pipelines, python-file jobs, notebooks&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Three execution profiles: Databricks, OSS spark-pipelines, Databricks Connect&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Deploy: DAB → GitHub OIDC → dev / stage / prod" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=22;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="172" width="520.0" height="274" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c5" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#4E7A88;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="182" width="5" height="254" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c6" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:14px;&#x27;&gt;DESIGN GOALS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• A target table = &lt;b&gt;ONE artifact&lt;/b&gt; (columns, dqx rules, CDC target) authored from natural language&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Framework vs domain&lt;/b&gt; strict separation — the framework lifts into any project untouched&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Single-writer invariant&lt;/b&gt; — every UC table has exactly one owning lane&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Config validated by Pydantic + dqx — the SAME loader in CI, pytest, and the pipeline&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• No hand-written &lt;tt&gt;dp.*&lt;/tt&gt; / MERGE unless the capability matrix says the framework cannot express it" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=22;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="590.0" y="172" width="520.0" height="274" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c7" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2A900;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="590.0" y="182" width="5" height="254" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c8" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:14px;&#x27;&gt;WHY (DRIVERS)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Config-driven beats hand-written pipelines — reviewable, statically validated, uniform across tables&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Data quality as &lt;b&gt;evidence&lt;/b&gt; — dqx valid/quarantine split with _errors structs&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Run anywhere&lt;/b&gt; — local OSS for a fast inner loop, Connect for live validation, Databricks for prod&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Reproducible deps — uv end to end (&lt;tt&gt;uv.lock&lt;/tt&gt;, CI &lt;tt&gt;--frozen&lt;/tt&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Agents author tables safely behind protected-file + branch-first guards" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=22;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1140.0" y="172" width="520.0" height="274" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c9" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FF3621;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1140.0" y="182" width="5" height="254" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c10" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:15px;&#x27;&gt;THE FLOWSPEC PATTERN  ·  config/&amp;lt;catalog&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;schema&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;table&amp;gt;.yml is the source of truth&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every target table is declared by ONE YAML artifact (file name == table name; folder path mirrors the UC namespace &lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt;catalog&amp;gt;.&amp;lt;schema&amp;gt;.&amp;lt;table&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;). The artifact declares:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ &lt;b&gt;source(s)&lt;/b&gt; — cloud_files / files / table / view / kafka (single &lt;tt&gt;source:&lt;/tt&gt; or fan-in &lt;tt&gt;sources:&lt;/tt&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ &lt;b&gt;columns&lt;/b&gt; — source→target names, data types (always &lt;tt&gt;try_cast&lt;/tt&gt;), per-column dqx rules&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ &lt;b&gt;transform&lt;/b&gt; steps (registry names) + table-level &lt;b&gt;quality&lt;/b&gt; checks&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ optional &lt;b&gt;backfill:&lt;/b&gt; once-flows (the recreation path + audit trail)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ &lt;b&gt;target&lt;/b&gt; kind — streaming_table [+cdc | +cdc_from_snapshot] / materialized_view / temporary_view / delta_sink / kafka_sink&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;datalab.framework.generate&lt;/b&gt; turns the validated config into Lakeflow SDP datasets. Business logic lives in &lt;tt&gt;src/&amp;lt;catalog&amp;gt;_etl/transforms/&lt;/tt&gt; as pure &lt;tt&gt;@transform&lt;/tt&gt; functions; custom dqx in &lt;tt&gt;checks/&lt;/tt&gt;. The per-domain &lt;tt&gt;transformations/pipeline.py&lt;/tt&gt; is 3 lines. &lt;b&gt;Never &lt;tt&gt;import dlt&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/b&gt; — this repo standardizes on &lt;tt&gt;pyspark.pipelines&lt;/tt&gt;." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=22;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="476" width="1620" height="226" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c11" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E8912A;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="486" width="5" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c12" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:13px;&#x27;&gt;How this file is structured&lt;/b&gt; — Pages 2-5 walk the flow:&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;AUTHOR&lt;/b&gt; (Page 2: artifact anatomy + the 3-question lane router) &amp;nbsp;→&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;GENERATE&lt;/b&gt; (Page 3: YAML → pyspark.pipelines datasets) &amp;nbsp;→&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;RUN&lt;/b&gt; (Page 4: medallion runtime + the three execution profiles) &amp;nbsp;→&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;SHIP&lt;/b&gt; (Page 5: bundle deploy + RBAC / ABAC governance)." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FDF6E9;strokeColor=#EBD6A8;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=16;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="722" width="1620" height="64" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c13" value="&lt;b&gt;The artifact is the contract. Author it; the framework owns materialization. Full reference + SDP capability matrix: docs/FRAMEWORK.md.  The implemented system is mapped in design/02_implementation_end_to_end.drawio.&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11.5;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="804" width="1620" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="xf-p2" name="2 - AUTHOR - Artifact + lane router">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1700" pageHeight="932" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="c1" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FF3621;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="40" width="54" height="5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c2" value="&lt;b&gt;STAGE 1 of 4 · AUTHOR · The YAML artifact anatomy + the 3-question lane router&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=24;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="54" width="1620" height="38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c3" value="Adding or changing a table = authoring its artifact, not writing Python. Use the author-ldp-artifact skill to turn a natural-language request into the YAML below. Route every new target through the 3-question router first." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13.5;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="98" width="1620" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c4" value="&lt;b&gt;A  ·  Artifact anatomy  —  config/&amp;lt;catalog&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;schema&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;table&amp;gt;.yml  (one file == one target table)&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0E1A20;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="154" width="1040" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c5" value="&lt;b&gt;B  ·  Route every new target — the 3-question router&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0E1A20;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1110" y="154" width="550" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c6" value="&lt;b&gt;source:&lt;/b&gt; / &lt;b&gt;sources:&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; one input or a fan-in list (replaces UNION).&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;kinds: &lt;tt&gt;cloud_files&lt;/tt&gt; (Auto Loader) · &lt;tt&gt;files&lt;/tt&gt; · &lt;tt&gt;table&lt;/tt&gt; · &lt;tt&gt;view&lt;/tt&gt; · &lt;tt&gt;kafka&lt;/tt&gt;. Each flow has a name — &lt;i&gt;flow names are streaming-checkpoint identities&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;columns:&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; the source→target mapping. &lt;tt&gt;name&lt;/tt&gt; / &lt;tt&gt;source&lt;/tt&gt; / &lt;tt&gt;type&lt;/tt&gt; (cast with &lt;tt&gt;try_cast&lt;/tt&gt; so ANSI-mode bad values become NULL, not a stream failure) + per-column &lt;b&gt;quality:&lt;/b&gt; dqx rules.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;transform:&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; ordered step list referencing &lt;tt&gt;@transform&lt;/tt&gt;-registered pure functions in the domain package.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;quality:&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; table-level dqx checks (dqx metadata format). One rules list drives BOTH the target filter and the &lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt;table&amp;gt;_quarantine&lt;/tt&gt; split.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;backfill:&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; optional once-flows (batch source; streaming when the target has &lt;tt&gt;cdc:&lt;/tt&gt;). They re-run on full refresh by design.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;target:&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; the kind + its options (see C below) — &lt;tt&gt;cdc&lt;/tt&gt; / &lt;tt&gt;cdc_from_snapshot&lt;/tt&gt; keys, sequence_by, SCD type." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=16;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="198" width="1040" height="242" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c7" value="&lt;b&gt;1.&lt;/b&gt; Is the output a managed Delta table in the medallion, derivable from upstream datasets?&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ &lt;b&gt;SDP&lt;/b&gt; (mandatory). Backfills included as &lt;tt&gt;backfill:&lt;/tt&gt; once-flows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2.&lt;/b&gt; Is it a side-effectful action (export to a volume / external system, API pull into landing, non-SDP table maintenance) running headless on a schedule?&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ &lt;b&gt;python-file&lt;/b&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;spark_python_task&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;src/jobs/&lt;/tt&gt;).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3.&lt;/b&gt; Must a human read the run output and decide?&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ &lt;b&gt;notebook&lt;/b&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;notebook_task&lt;/tt&gt;, on-demand only — no trigger).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;When in doubt: SDP. Exploration with no managed target stays out of the bundle.&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=16;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1110" y="198" width="550" height="218" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c8" value="&lt;b&gt;Single-writer invariant + don&#x27;ts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Every UC table has exactly ONE owning lane. Jobs and notebooks may READ SDP-owned tables, never WRITE them — a &lt;tt&gt;.saveAsTable&lt;/tt&gt; on an SDP streaming table corrupts pipeline state.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Repaired / backfill data re-enters via the landing volume or a &lt;tt&gt;backfill:&lt;/tt&gt; flow — never a job write.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• No &lt;tt&gt;import dlt&lt;/tt&gt;, no hand-written MERGE, no hardcoded catalogs/paths (use pipeline &lt;tt&gt;configuration&lt;/tt&gt; + &lt;tt&gt;pipeline_conf&lt;/tt&gt;)." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FDEDEB;strokeColor=#F0B9B1;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=22;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1110" y="432" width="550" height="202" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c9" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FF3621;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1110" y="442" width="5" height="182" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c10" value="&lt;b&gt;C  ·  Target kinds (the YAML target: block) — the SDP surface the framework can express&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0E1A20;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="664" width="1620" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c11" value="&lt;b&gt;streaming_table&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;tt&gt;@dp.table&lt;/tt&gt;, append/streaming ingest (Auto Loader, Kafka).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;|&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;streaming_table + cdc&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;tt&gt;create_streaming_table&lt;/tt&gt; + &lt;tt&gt;create_auto_cdc_flow&lt;/tt&gt; (keys + sequence_by; SCD1/SCD2) — replaces MERGE.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;streaming_table + cdc_from_snapshot&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;tt&gt;create_auto_cdc_from_snapshot_flow&lt;/tt&gt; for periodic FULL dumps (nightly extracts).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;|&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;materialized_view&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;tt&gt;@dp.materialized_view&lt;/tt&gt; (gold aggregates, batch).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;temporary_view&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;tt&gt;@dp.temporary_view&lt;/tt&gt; (pipeline-scoped).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;|&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;delta_sink&lt;/b&gt; / &lt;b&gt;kafka_sink&lt;/b&gt; — streaming publish (append-only; never cleared by full refresh, so &lt;tt&gt;backfill:&lt;/tt&gt; is rejected on sinks).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Anything the matrix says is genuinely out of scope (e.g. Kinesis / Pub/Sub sources) is the rare case for the author-sdp-pipeline skill — extend the framework first.&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=16;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="708" width="1620" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c12" value="&lt;b&gt;Author the artifact, add any new @transform with a unit test, then: make validate-configs lint test validate. Verify interactively with run_dataset / make validate-connect — no deploy needed.&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11.5;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="866" width="1620" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="xf-p3" name="3 - GENERATE - YAML to SDP">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1700" pageHeight="914" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="c1" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FF3621;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="40" width="54" height="5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c2" value="&lt;b&gt;STAGE 2 of 4 · GENERATE · datalab.framework turns the YAML into pyspark.pipelines datasets&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=24;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="54" width="1620" height="38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c3" value="The same loader runs in CI, pytest (local Spark) and the deployed pipeline. Dataset functions RETURN a DataFrame — the engine owns materialization (no .write / .saveAsTable / .start / .collect inside them)." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13.5;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="98" width="1620" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c4" value="&lt;b&gt;1 · models.py&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pydantic config contract.&lt;br&gt;Parses + validates every artifact (and domain.yml).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;make validate-configs fails fast on a bad rule or type.&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=22;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="154" width="352.5" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c5" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#4E7A88;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="164" width="5" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c6" value="&lt;b&gt;2 · loader.py + registry&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Reads domain.yml imports; resolves &lt;tt&gt;@transform&lt;/tt&gt; / &lt;tt&gt;@check_function&lt;/tt&gt; / &lt;tt&gt;@snapshot_source&lt;/tt&gt; by name.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Framework hardcodes no domain module.&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=22;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="462.5" y="154" width="352.5" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c7" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#4E7A88;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="462.5" y="164" width="5" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c8" value="&lt;b&gt;3 · generator.generate()&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Builds the graph: readers → column map (try_cast) → transform steps → dqx → target.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Routes on &lt;tt&gt;datalab.profile&lt;/tt&gt; (see the profile box below)." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=22;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="885.0" y="154" width="352.5" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c9" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#4E7A88;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="885.0" y="164" width="5" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c10" value="&lt;b&gt;4 · SDP datasets&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;tt&gt;@dp.table&lt;/tt&gt; (streaming)&lt;br&gt;&lt;tt&gt;@dp.materialized_view&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;tt&gt;create_streaming_table&lt;/tt&gt; + &lt;tt&gt;create_auto_cdc_flow&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Functions return a DataFrame.&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=22;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1307.5" y="154" width="352.5" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c11" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2A900;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1307.5" y="164" width="5" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c12" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeColor=#5A6B7B;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1.0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#000000;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c4" target="c6">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c13" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeColor=#5A6B7B;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1.0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#000000;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c6" target="c8">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c14" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeColor=#5A6B7B;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1.0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#000000;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c8" target="c10">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c15" value="&lt;b&gt;Profile routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;tt&gt;datalab.profile&lt;/tt&gt;:&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;databricks&lt;/b&gt; → dp.* datasets (default)&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;local&lt;/b&gt; → batch materialized views (framework/local.py)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;tt&gt;compat.py&lt;/tt&gt; guards Databricks-only knobs locally." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E8F1F8;strokeColor=#B7CFE0;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=16;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="885.0" y="338" width="352.5" height="156" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c16" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeColor=#5A6B7B;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#000000;dashed=1;dashPattern=6 5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c15" target="c8">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c17" value="&lt;b&gt;dqx data quality  —  ONE rules list drives valid + quarantine (dp.expect_* is retired here)&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0E1A20;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="524" width="1620" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c18" value="&lt;b&gt;framework/dq.py&lt;/b&gt; routes the artifact&#x27;s &lt;tt&gt;quality.checks&lt;/tt&gt; through databrickslabs/dqx.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;criticality: error&lt;/b&gt; rows are dropped from the target and land in &lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt;dataset&amp;gt;_quarantine&lt;/tt&gt; with &lt;tt&gt;_errors&lt;/tt&gt; evidence structs; &lt;b&gt;warn&lt;/b&gt; rows flow through flagged.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Default &lt;tt&gt;quarantine.include_warnings: false&lt;/tt&gt; keeps quarantine == exactly the dropped rows. With fan-in &lt;tt&gt;sources:&lt;/tt&gt; every flow feeds the same quarantine. Optional &lt;tt&gt;*_dq_metrics&lt;/tt&gt; MV. Locally dqx runs with a mocked WorkspaceClient and static run_time / run_id overwrites (removing them breaks MV incrementalization)." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=22;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="568" width="1620" height="94" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c19" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FF3621;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="578" width="5" height="74" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c20" value="&lt;b&gt;AUTO CDC  —  upserts without MERGE (the engine owns the merge)&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0E1A20;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="692" width="1620" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c21" value="&lt;tt&gt;target.cdc&lt;/tt&gt; → &lt;tt&gt;create_streaming_table&lt;/tt&gt; + &lt;tt&gt;create_auto_cdc_flow(target=..., source=..., keys=[...], sequence_by=...)&lt;/tt&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;tt&gt;target.cdc_from_snapshot&lt;/tt&gt; → &lt;tt&gt;create_auto_cdc_from_snapshot_flow&lt;/tt&gt; for periodic full snapshots.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Flow names are checkpoint identities — renaming a fan-in / backfill flow (or converting single-source ↔ fan-in) abandons state and reprocesses from scratch; pair such a change with a deliberate full refresh. Streaming FROM a CDC/SCD table needs &lt;tt&gt;options: {skipChangeCommits: true}&lt;/tt&gt;." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#C9D2DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=22;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="736" width="1620" height="94" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c22" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#4E7A88;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="746" width="5" height="74" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c23" value="&lt;b&gt;The framework is an external dependency: change it in the datalab-framework repo (its docs/FRAMEWORK.md is the doc of record); after a framework bump, make sync-schemas regenerates the vendored schemas/*.json.&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11.5;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="848" width="1620" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="xf-p4" name="4 - RUN - Medallion + profiles">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1700" pageHeight="824" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="c1" value="" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FF3621;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
